Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 19:09:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Remove Lovable platform dependency and branding
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Rewrites vite.config.ts as a standalone config, no longer wrapped by
@lovable.dev/vite-tanstack-config. Read that package's actual source
before rewriting to confirm parity: it replicates TanStack devtools
(dev-only), Tailwind, tsconfig path aliases, TanStack Start, Nitro
(build-only, Cloudflare preset), React, and the same dedupe/watch
settings. Deliberately does NOT replicate the Lovable-sandbox-only
pieces (asset proxy, HMR gate, dev-server bridge, bundled-dev CSS shim,
build error diagnostics) — confirmed via source that all of these were
already no-ops outside a Lovable sandbox (gated behind
LOVABLE_SANDBOX/DEV_SERVER__PROJECT_PATH env checks), so nothing
functional is lost.

Also removes:
- .lovable/ (Lovable's internal plan/project-state tracking)
- AGENTS.md (contained only a Lovable git-history-sync warning)
- src/lib/lovable-error-reporting.ts and its use in __root.tsx's error
  boundary (reported client errors to a Lovable-injected
  window.__lovableEvents hook that doesn't exist outside the Lovable
  editor)
- @lovable.dev/vite-tanstack-config from package.json; promotes
  @tanstack/devtools-vite (previously only transitive) to a direct
  devDependency since vite.config.ts now imports it explicitly
- Lovable package names from bunfig.toml's supply-chain-guard exclude
  list
- "Connect Supabase in Lovable Cloud" wording in the three Supabase
  client env-var error messages (client.ts, client.server.ts,
  auth-middleware.ts), replaced with a generic "set them in your .env
  file" message
- stale "This file is automatically generated. Do not edit it
  directly." headers on the same three files — inaccurate now that
  Lovable's codegen no longer touches them, and misleading to a future
  editor (human or AI) who might assume changes get overwritten. The
  genuinely CLI-generated src/integrations/supabase/types.ts is
  untouched.

Verified: after `npm install` (net -2 packages), `tsc --noEmit` and
`eslint` both pass with no new issues, and — the real test, since this
touches the build pipeline — a full `vite build` succeeds and produces
the same Cloudflare Worker output shape (wrangler.json, nitro.json,
_headers) as before. Also booted the dev server on the new config and
confirmed via live HTTP requests that env vars still load correctly
without Lovable's manual `envDefine` step (Vite's native .env loading
was already sufficient) and that the route-nesting fix from the
previous commit still holds.
